# construction/fleet-roster.kyri -- the fleet's one seat table.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The binding seat -> tree -> engine is the fleet's only real datum, and it
# was spelled in six independent places across two executables: fleet-loop.sh's allow-list, its
# want_tree case, its FLEET_DRY case and its run_lap case, plus fleet_rearm.sh's report_seat rows
# and its relaunch case. Nothing compared them, and by `20260904` two had already drifted -- the
# loop admitted six seat names while the re-arm reported nine, and the elder-name remap seated on
# Keaton's word lived in one file and not the other. A rule written six times is a rule six files
# may quietly come to disagree about; this is that rule written once.
#
# THE SHAPE is the standing roster's own: a record opens with `seat` and carries plain key-value
# lines until the next one. Read it with tools/fixtures/f/fleet_roster_scan.sh rather than by
# grepping here, so one parse serves sh, Rishi, and the launcher prose alike.
#
# STATUS is the field that lets an elder seat stay readable without pretending it runs. `live` is
# a seat the fleet sails today; `parked` is one whose tree no host currently holds, kept by name
# because it may sail again and because an absent directory is a filesystem accident where a
# parked row is a declaration. fleet_rearm.sh already reports an absent tree honestly; this makes
# that honesty something a reader can check against intent.
#
# ELDER names the seat's prior spelling, so a hand who types the old word is corrected rather than
# refused. The word is retired from the seat name, never from the reader's muscle memory.
format fleet-roster-v1

# -- the three Earth ships, names seated 20260904 on Keaton's word ----------------------------
seat incense
tree grain-incense
engine claude
lane law, active-designing, iterative review, and the captain's hat
status live
seated 20260904.013013

seat pheromone
tree grain-pheromone
engine claude
lane the molecular star -- the language details a rune wants
elder furrow
status live
seated 20260904.013013

seat petrichor
tree grain-petrichor
engine claude
lane docs-geode (tend, never rename) and prose-product
elder harvest
status live
seated 20260904.013013

# -- the aether seats, parked. Their charter stays testimony at
# active-designing/20260829-203718_the-six-bodies-and-the-always-fleet.md, and every law it earned
# -- one tree per star, claim-as-override, the ruling seats -- the Earth trio inherits whole.
seat silence
tree grain-silence
engine claude
lane the infrastructure half of Grain in Glow
status parked
seated 20260829.203718

seat hush
tree grain-hush
engine claude
lane Pond completes the enclosure, under the accrete-only boundary
status parked
seated 20260829.203718

seat dream
tree grain-dream
engine codex
lane the systems core -- Caravan, Tally, the Scribe seams
status parked
seated 20260829.203718

# The interactive field sitting. It runs no unattended loop, which is why `engine field` is its
# own word rather than a blank: a seat with no engine would read as a row somebody forgot to
# finish, and this one is finished.
seat sound
tree grain
engine field
lane the interactive bench -- Glow language custody, and where rulings land
status parked
seated 20260829.203718
